# TOP-INSTAL Core Context Router

This is the only always-on Cursor rule in this repo. Keep it short. Detailed procedures live in workspace skills and runbooks.

## Default Token Discipline

- Use Caveman-lite by default: compact, professional, no filler.
- Keep code, commands, paths, IDs, logs, errors, and proof language exact.
- Do not compress safety-critical warnings or irreversible-action confirmations.
- CodeBurn is default local cost observability; never treat it as runtime proof.

## Authority Order

1. `AGENTS.md` (this repo) and `../../AGENTS.md` (workspace constitution).
2. `../../knowledge/INDEX.md` and `../../knowledge/source-of-truth.md` for cross-repo routing.
3. `docs/core/PROJECT_README.md`, `docs/runbooks/LAST_PROVEN_STATE.md` — repo canon; LPS only for proof/runtime claims.
4. `../../knowledge/system-atlas/tooling/agent-harness/AGENT_DEVELOPMENT_HARNESS.md` — when harness/MCP/proof workflow is in scope.
5. `../../knowledge/system-atlas/tooling/agent-harness/AGENT_SKILLS_REGISTRY.md` — pick 1-3 skills.
6. `../../.agents/skills/<skill>/SKILL.md` — open only selected skills.
7. `references/` under the selected skill — only when required.
8. Source files and tests — after scope is narrow.

## Non-Negotiable Boundaries

- Node A = WordPress / Daszek / operator surface / REST endpoints / JSONL projection storage (`../../daszek/`).
- Node B = `gmail-agent` Python runtime / Postgres / pgvector / policy / workers.
- Node A and Node B communicate through HTTP/REST bridge, not shared filesystem.
- Daszek is projection-only, not source of truth.
- `gmail-agent` owns Gmail intake, mailbox memory, policy, reconciliation, and Daszek projection feed.
- `kalk-top` owns HVAC calculation, selection, pricing, and `OfferDTO`.
- Local files are not live proof of VPS, WordPress, Gmail, Drive, Postgres, or Gate B.

## Git i repo (always-on)

- Read-oriented `git status`, `git diff`, `git log` are OK for orientation.
- Writes (commit, push, merge): operator intent or `scripts/ai_os_task.py` from workspace root.
- Do not commit secrets or ignored files.

## Conflict resolution

- `../../knowledge/memory/OPERATOR_DECISIONS.md` supersedes repo rules.
- VPS/prod: explicit operator request only — see workspace `05-local-only-mandate.mdc`.

## Context Loading

Before non-trivial work: read task, `AGENTS.md`, workspace `AGENTS.md` when cross-repo, and LPS only for proof claims. Select at most 1-3 skills from the workspace registry. Do not load `memory-bank/`, `.claude/**`, `.gitnexus/**`, archives, or broad doc trees by default.

## Skill Router (names → workspace `.agents/skills/`)

`karpathy-guidelines` (repo rule `karpathy-guidelines.mdc`); then as needed:

`cursor-codex-harness`, `topinstal-node-topology`, `gmail-agent-proof-run`, `policy-action-gates`, `agent-skill-quality-gate`.

Backlog skills: see registry; do not assume they exist until listed as active.

## Hard Rule

Do not turn Cursor rules into a second `AGENTS.md`. If a task matches a skill, use the skill. Proof → `gmail-agent-proof-run`. Code graph → `CODE_INTELLIGENCE_ROUTER.md` at workspace. Coding discipline → `karpathy-guidelines.mdc`.

## MCP and tooling anti-drift (always-on)

- Prefer workspace `CODE_INTELLIGENCE_ROUTER.md` before adding MCP servers.
- Request order: narrow reads + LSP → `just`/CLI → repo-assistant MCP → allowed workspace MCP → never forbidden servers.
- Prefer code execution (`pytest`, `gmail_intake.py`, workspace `preflight-local-stack.ps1`) over widening MCP.
- Treat MCP output as hints; verify with source reads and tests.
- Markdown links in `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` resolve relative to this folder — use `../../` for workspace paths.
- After harness edits: `python ../../scripts/context_link_audit.py --scope gmail-agent` from workspace root.
